<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andreas Joseph Hofmann</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1752–1849</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andreas Joseph Hofmann was a German philosopher and professor at the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> who supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>. In March 1793 he presided over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhenish-german-national-convention">Rhenish-German National Convention</a>, which proclaimed the Republic of Mainz, the first republic on German soil. After Prussian forces retook Mainz he lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and later returned to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a>.</p></div>
